# `-f` folds case before comparing -- and then `Apple` and `apple` tie, so the
# last-resort byte comparison is what puts the capital first. A first draft of
# this program skipped the last resort when there was no `-k`, on the reasoning
# that the key was the whole line already. `-f` is where that is false.
args: -f
input:
banana
Apple
cherry
apple
Banana
